"MA-2": {"statement":[{"label":"a.","prose":"Schedule, document, and review records of maintenance, repair, and replacement on system components in accordance with manufacturer or vendor specifications and/or organizational requirements;"},{"label":"b.","prose":"Approve and monitor all maintenance activities, whether performed on site or remotely and whether the system or system components are serviced on site or removed to another location;"},{"label":"c.","prose":"Require that [Assignment: organization-defined personnel or roles] explicitly approve the removal of the system or system components from organizational facilities for off-site maintenance, repair, or replacement;"},{"label":"d.","prose":"Sanitize equipment to remove the following information from associated media prior to removal from organizational facilities for off-site maintenance, repair, or replacement: [Assignment: organization-defined information];"},{"label":"e.","prose":"Check all potentially impacted controls to verify that the controls are still functioning properly following maintenance, repair, or replacement actions; and"},{"label":"f.","prose":"Include the following information in organizational maintenance records: [Assignment: organization-defined information]."}],"discussion":["Controlling system maintenance addresses the information security aspects of the system maintenance program and applies to all types of maintenance to system components conducted by local or nonlocal entities. Maintenance includes peripherals such as scanners, copiers, and printers. Information necessary for creating effective maintenance records includes the date and time of maintenance, a description of the maintenance performed, names of the individuals or group performing the maintenance, name of the escort, and system components or equipment that are removed or replaced. Organizations consider supply chain-related risks associated with replacement components for systems."],"params":[{"id":"MA-02_ODP[01]","kind":"Assignment","value":"[Assignment: organization-defined personnel or roles]","guideline":"personnel or roles required to explicitly approve the removal of the system or system components from organizational facilities for off-site maintenance or repairs is/are defined"},{"id":"MA-02_ODP[02]","kind":"Assignment","value":"[Assignment: organization-defined information]","guideline":"information to be removed from associated media prior to removal from organizational facilities for off-site maintenance, repair, or replacement is defined"},{"id":"MA-02_ODP[03]","kind":"Assignment","value":"[Assignment: organization-defined information]","guideline":"information to be included in organizational maintenance records is defined"}],"related":["CM-2","CM-3","CM-4","CM-5","CM-8","MA-4","MP-6","PE-16","SI-2","SR-3","SR-4","SR-11"],"objectives":[{"id":"ma-2_obj.a","label":"MA-02a.","prose":"","items":[{"id":"ma-2_obj.a-1","label":"MA-02a.[01]","prose":"maintenance, repair, and replacement of system components are scheduled in accordance with manufacturer or vendor specifications and/or organizational requirements;"},{"id":"ma-2_obj.a-2","label":"MA-02a.[02]","prose":"maintenance, repair, and replacement of system components are documented in accordance with manufacturer or vendor specifications and/or organizational requirements;"},{"id":"ma-2_obj.a-3","label":"MA-02a.[03]","prose":"records of maintenance, repair, and replacement of system components are reviewed in accordance with manufacturer or vendor specifications and/or organizational requirements;"}]},{"id":"ma-2_obj.b","label":"MA-02b.","prose":"","items":[{"id":"ma-2_obj.b-1","label":"MA-02b.[01]","prose":"all maintenance activities, whether performed on site or remotely and whether the system or system components are serviced on site or removed to another location, are approved;"},{"id":"ma-2_obj.b-2","label":"MA-02b.[02]","prose":"all maintenance activities, whether performed on site or remotely and whether the system or system components are serviced on site or removed to another location, are monitored;"}]},{"id":"ma-2_obj.c","label":"MA-02c.","prose":"[Assignment: organization-defined personnel or roles] is/are required to explicitly approve the removal of the system or system components from organizational facilities for off-site maintenance, repair, or replacement;"},{"id":"ma-2_obj.d","label":"MA-02d.","prose":"equipment is sanitized to remove [Assignment: organization-defined information] from associated media prior to removal from organizational facilities for off-site maintenance, repair, or replacement;"},{"id":"ma-2_obj.e","label":"MA-02e.","prose":"all potentially impacted controls are checked to verify that the controls are still functioning properly following maintenance, repair, or replacement actions;"},{"id":"ma-2_obj.f","label":"MA-02f.","prose":"[Assignment: organization-defined information] is included in organizational maintenance records."}],"methods":[{"method":"Examine","objects":["Maintenance policy","procedures addressing controlled system maintenance","maintenance records","manufacturer/vendor maintenance specifications","equipment sanitization records","media sanitization records","system security plan","other relevant documents or records"]},{"method":"Interview","objects":["Organizational personnel with system maintenance responsibilities","organizational personnel with information security responsibilities","organizational personnel responsible for media sanitization","system/network administrators"]},{"method":"Test","objects":["Organizational processes for scheduling, performing, documenting, reviewing, approving, and monitoring maintenance and repairs for the system","organizational processes for sanitizing system components","mechanisms supporting and/or implementing controlled maintenance","mechanisms implementing the sanitization of system components"]}],"references":[{"title":"OMB A-130","url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/sites/whitehouse.gov/files/omb/circulars/A130/a130revised.pdf"},{"title":"IR 8023","url":"https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.IR.8023"}]},
